    <summary type="html"><![CDATA[<p><strong>Bot Screen / Desktop Passthrough Launch</strong> — the dominant story of the batch: <strong>@NousResearch</strong> unveiled <strong><a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-ef6b4179c4fa" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bot Screen for Hermes Desktop</a></strong> (real-time streaming of any agent session) while <strong>Teknium</strong> announced <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-4784626f2a61" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">live visual/interactive desktop passthrough for Hermes Agent</a> (1,133 likes, ~173k views), backed by official docs and a <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-d84a2bc0a85d" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">community walkthrough from @tonbistudio</a>. Sentiment was euphoric and long-awaited — Teknium's <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-014ad26a44c6" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">'Finallllly!'</a> and <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-48968e1c836e" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">'Much needed!'</a> (~20k views) captured pent-up demand, with <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-14f5c1982517" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">hype replies amplifying the launch thread</a>. <strong>oh-my-hermes (OMH) &amp; Jev Ecosystem</strong> — <strong>rlaope</strong> delivered the batch's strongest engagement (1,706 views) announcing <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-415aecf318f8" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">OMH support for Jev-Skills and model routing</a>, then open-sourced <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-8530d32deea5" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">jeval</a> (Jev evaluation/visualization) and an updated <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-99948938337f" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">oh-my-hermes Plus</a>, positioning <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-b4d141253a4f" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">OMH as the all-in-one plugin for AI-native hermes-agent power users</a>. <strong>Usage Tips &amp; Guidance</strong> — the official account shared a practical gem: <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-768697783517" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">use Hermes via iMessage</a> with whichever model you prefer (~13k views), plus <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-d03d44ef66a9" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">pointers to walkthrough content</a>. <strong>Community Support &amp; Maintenance</strong> — <strong>Teknium</strong> stayed visibly hands-on: <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-d5a2f794eeec" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">disputing a cache complaint pending a reproducible issue</a>, celebrating a quick <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-3e1742f36c0b" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">'fixed lol' resolution</a>, and clarifying a <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-992950038a21" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">discussed tool was built by the Nous/Hermes team, not Anthropic</a>. <strong>Broader chatter</strong> — a <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-797e0ee6c95e" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">lukewarm take praising Opus 5.5 while questioning Claude Code's agent experience</a>, <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-921e5927b0af" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub show-and-tell prompts</a>, and short reaction posts rounding out a highly engaged, launch-driven week.</p>]]></summary>
    <content type="html"><![CDATA[<p><strong>Bot Screen / Desktop Passthrough Launch</strong> — the dominant story of the batch: <strong>@NousResearch</strong> unveiled <strong><a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-ef6b4179c4fa" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bot Screen for Hermes Desktop</a></strong> (real-time streaming of any agent session) while <strong>Teknium</strong> announced <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-4784626f2a61" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">live visual/interactive desktop passthrough for Hermes Agent</a> (1,133 likes, ~173k views), backed by official docs and a <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-d84a2bc0a85d" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">community walkthrough from @tonbistudio</a>. Sentiment was euphoric and long-awaited — Teknium's <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-014ad26a44c6" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">'Finallllly!'</a> and <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-48968e1c836e" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">'Much needed!'</a> (~20k views) captured pent-up demand, with <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-14f5c1982517" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">hype replies amplifying the launch thread</a>. <strong>oh-my-hermes (OMH) &amp; Jev Ecosystem</strong> — <strong>rlaope</strong> delivered the batch's strongest engagement (1,706 views) announcing <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-415aecf318f8" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">OMH support for Jev-Skills and model routing</a>, then open-sourced <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=s